# L §4.4 (tally 2.1.8 R13, X1; c3n x2): the first unknown day the answer carries, the first its reads met, is taken
# first, and each run again: w1 = 2026-03-05 decides the or, so w2 is not taken there. Taking both at once would
# print [w1 = 2026-03-05, w2 = ...]. The same lines as 2.1.7's refcore: a guard on the order.
=== m.tally
model t
  tally 2
  on 2026-01-01
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-06-30

source s "s"
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01
place konto: accounts PLN lives 2025-01-01..
place world: outside lives 1900-01-01..
input amt: money PLN
input w1: date
input w2: date
input w3: date
input a: date
input b[d in days]: date

move m1: transfers
  on w1
  leg cash from world to konto amount amt

move m2: transfers
  on w2
  leg cash from world to konto amount amt

move m3: transfers
  on w3
  leg cash from world to konto amount amt

version v
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2025-12-01
  amt = 100.00 PLN "s"
  w1 = window(2026-03-05, 2026-03-07) "s"
  w2 = window(2026-03-06, 2026-03-08) "s"
  w3 = window(2026-05-01, 2026-05-03) "s"
  a = window(2026-03-01, 2026-03-02) "s"
  b[2026-03-01] = window(2026-04-01, 2026-04-02) "s"
  b[2026-03-02] = 2026-05-01 "s"
  opening[konto] = 0.00 PLN at 2026-01-01 start "s"

ask x1: (w1 < 2026-03-06) or (w2 > 2026-03-07)
ask x2: (w1 < 2026-03-06) or (w2 > 2026-03-07) windows each
=== expect
x1: ?"date within window(2026-03-05, 2026-03-07) not precise enough for w1 < 2026-03-06" (w1) ?"date within window(2026-03-06, 2026-03-08) not precise enough for w2 > 2026-03-07" (w2)
  cut 2026-01-01
x2 [w1 = 2026-03-05]: true
  cut 2026-01-01
x2 [w1 = 2026-03-06 .. 2026-03-07, w2 = 2026-03-06 .. 2026-03-07]: false
  cut 2026-01-01
x2 [w1 = 2026-03-06 .. 2026-03-07, w2 = 2026-03-08]: true
  cut 2026-01-01
warning: WARN-UNREAD input a is read by nothing
warning: WARN-UNREAD input b is read by nothing
